WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.583
(upbeat music)

00:00:07.251 --> 00:00:09.115
- So whenever my mom goes to Nigeria,

00:00:09.115 --> 00:00:11.012
I always have her bring
me back some prints

00:00:11.012 --> 00:00:12.922
because it makes me feel closer to home

00:00:12.922 --> 00:00:14.191
and I just love to mix African prints.

00:00:14.191 --> 00:00:15.308
I think there's nothing like it.

00:00:15.308 --> 00:00:16.556
- This dress is my mother's.

00:00:16.556 --> 00:00:17.864
She got it in the 80's.

00:00:17.864 --> 00:00:19.589
She was my age when she lived in Senegal.

00:00:19.589 --> 00:00:21.414
Every time I wear something
connected to my culture,

00:00:21.414 --> 00:00:22.930
it feels right and it feels like

00:00:22.930 --> 00:00:24.447
what I want to do every day, honestly.

00:00:24.447 --> 00:00:27.239
- I bought everything that
I'm wearing from 125th Street,

00:00:27.239 --> 00:00:29.237
but African print has always been in

00:00:29.237 --> 00:00:30.809
because it comes straight
from the mother land

00:00:30.809 --> 00:00:33.400
and if you don't know,
you better ask somebody.

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:35.128
- I'm wearing an African print style today

00:00:35.128 --> 00:00:36.363
to represent my culture.

00:00:36.363 --> 00:00:37.922
I grew up in Kenyan culture my whole life.

00:00:37.922 --> 00:00:40.978
- I'm celebrating my
mother-f***ing heritage,

00:00:40.978 --> 00:00:43.264
and I am happy to be wearing it today.

00:00:43.264 --> 00:00:45.846
- [Guest] Wow, that's
my design. I made it.

00:00:45.846 --> 00:00:49.110
My mom sold African print for 35 years,

00:00:49.110 --> 00:00:51.862
so that was the only
thing I knew the most.

00:00:51.862 --> 00:00:54.675
That's how I showed how different I was.

00:00:54.675 --> 00:00:56.386
- My outfit is from East Africa,

00:00:56.386 --> 00:00:57.844
more specifically, Tanzania.

00:00:57.844 --> 00:00:59.669
- [Guest] Too often we forget

00:00:59.669 --> 00:01:02.047
we're really coming from Africa.

00:01:02.047 --> 00:01:05.528
We still have all this
culture ingrained in us.

00:01:05.528 --> 00:01:07.181
- Wearing these types of styles helps me

00:01:07.181 --> 00:01:10.061
feel like I am a little bit closer to home

00:01:10.061 --> 00:01:13.022
even though I live here, I
have another home in Tanzania.

00:01:13.022 --> 00:01:14.635
- Yes, it makes me feel
connected to my heritage.

00:01:14.635 --> 00:01:15.675
It's loud. It's proud.

00:01:15.675 --> 00:01:16.508
It's brilliant.

00:01:16.508 --> 00:01:17.919
- It's like being able to have

00:01:17.919 --> 00:01:19.645
a little bit of home everywhere I go.

00:01:19.645 --> 00:01:21.034
- Even if you're born
here, first generation,

00:01:21.034 --> 00:01:23.137
second, third generation,
you should always make sure

00:01:23.137 --> 00:01:24.953
that you're connected to your heritage,

00:01:24.953 --> 00:01:26.182
- [Third Guest] because in order
to know where you're going,

00:01:26.182 --> 00:01:27.745
you must know where you come from.

00:01:27.745 --> 00:01:30.685
And wearing these prints and
collectively understanding

00:01:30.685 --> 00:01:33.267
the story and the messaging
behind the prints,

00:01:33.267 --> 00:01:36.071
understanding the significance
of representing our culture,

00:01:36.071 --> 00:01:37.992
representing our continent.

00:01:37.992 --> 00:01:40.575
(upbeat music)

